    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Math is my favorite subject—it’s like solving puzzles, and I love the way it makes sense of the world. My physics classes make me see how math is everywhere, from motion to energy. It’s challenging but rewarding, especially when I finally get it. I’ve been teaching myself more since I dropped out of school, and it’s been a fun journey. My mom, who has a master’s, helped me with some tough concepts, but I still struggle with consistency because of my part-time job. Still, I’m hooked on learning more.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yeah, sometimes I do. When I hit a problem that’s too complex, my mind goes blank, and I start doubting myself. It’s not just the math—it’s the pressure I put on myself to understand everything perfectly. I get frustrated easily, especially when I can’t see the solution right away. But I’ve learned to take breaks, listen to classical music, or even do some yoga to calm down. It’s a work in progress, though—I’m still figuring out how to handle the stress better.",
